From b817f2d1574483a57546fffa563515b54f9b6052 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ewan McIntyre <ewan3568@me.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 01:06:01 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Trip builder: new-trip email with the whole trip + Approve /
 Not approved / Edit it

The email the crew gets for a new trip request now shows everything the guest built:
who they are, dates, every stop with its tours and the travel between, the money
(including a suggested balance), a heads-up list and their note. Three buttons open
a crew review page in the trip builder where the crew can approve (send the balance
link), decline (optional refund) or edit the trip and save the crew's version.

- email.ts: new tripBuilderOpsEmail layout; ready email links the checked plan
- trip-builder-crew.ts: signed per-trip links (HMAC, 30 days, one trip), safe summary reader
- trip-builder-admin: view / revise / link actions; crew key accepted for one open trip
- trip-builder-request: store the crew brief as the itinerary text
- trip-builder-test-emails: sample request MM-SAMPLE so the buttons work in the test send
- Admin > Trip builder: Review page button
- public/trip-builder: crew.js, ui-crew.js, crew.css, logic.js, CREW_ENDPOINT
- optional TRIP_BUILDER_TEAM_EMAILS to copy the team

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
